612605,"donor_log2fc":0.115091,"donor_lfcse":0.0579258,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.0445557}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000100226","entrez_id":["9567"],"uniprot":["O00178"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene is upregulated by interferon-gamma and encodes a protein that is a member of the AGP11/GTPBP1 family of GTP-binding proteins. A structurally similar protein has been found in mouse, where disruption of the gene for that protein had no observable phenotype. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O00178","text":"GTPase that plays a role in the elongation phase of protein synthesis by forming ternary complexes with GTP and aminoacyl-transfer RNAs (aa-tRNAs), and delivering aa-tRNAs to the ribosomal A site in a GTP-dependent manner (PubMed:30108131). Is also able to deliver deacylated tRNA to the A site (PubMed:30108131). Additionally, it is involved in RNA quality control; after GTP hydrolysis, which is not immediately followed by rapid peptide bond formation, GTPBP1 likely retains aa-tRNA in the A site and promotes exosomal degradation of faulty mRNAs engaged in 80S elongation complexes (PubMed:30108131). Plays a role in the regulation of circadian mRNA stability (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}